     "title": "dash task rfc-check gives one stable score for one change",
     "description": "(@nha, 2026-11-09: « we probably want a pass to ensure we follow the rust RFC. ») PR 1480 scored 0.44, 0.51, 0.47 as moves changed only the diff's chunk boundaries; the 0.5 bar read noise as a breach (2026-11-12).\n\n**Done when**\n\n1. The same change split into different chunks scores within 0.02; a test with PR 1480's three heads as fixtures. 2. A score within 0.05 of the bar names the part that decided it and is read twice; a test. 3. After merge: dash task rfc-check 1480 prints the same score three runs in a row.\n\nsite_perso: `rust-rfc-check-stable`",
