     "title": "A test attribute adds the test budget itself; no line to forget",
     "description": "(@nha, 2026-11-12: « always aim for the systemic improvement not the cheap one-off ») Three tasks lost a commit attempt on 2026-11-12 to the gate's « every test needs TestBudget » (apply-greenhouse, monitors-port, an earlier one).\n\n**Done when**\n\n1. A #\\[dash_test\\] attribute (or a nextest setup) gives every test its budget; a test proves a test without the line still runs inside it. 2. The workspace's tests use it; every_rule_opens_with_its_guard no longer asks for the line; a test. 3. After merge: a week of task commits shows no refusal for a missing budget.\n\nsite_perso: `rust-test-budget-attr`",
